  "notes": "Bayly's A A' B A' form (16 bars). A/A' from the Musica Viva ABC (K:F, chords F/C/C7) transposed F->C; incipit 1-1-2-3-3-4-5-6-5-3 confirmed by hymnary.org. B section (bars 9-12: 5-4-3-2-low5 | 4-3-2-1, twice) from the Elias Howe 1844 ABC and the Lester Bailey ABC (G->C), with repeated-note syllable splits and instrumental fills dropped. No pickup. Old version was a different, invented melody (wrong from bar 1). Chords: C C G G7-C | C C G7 C | G7 G7-C G7 G7-C | C C G7 C. LH: root half + 3rd/5th dyad, final C triad."
